posts.body:
If you're under time pressure, I'd recommend against trying to get this to work. There's a good chance you won't succeed in doing so, especially with transitioning back to the regular RM game. Put your time into making things you know you can do.
mono443 said:
Why showing errors when it's working perfectly?
Click to expand...
I'm not sure why you're surprised by this. It does indeed work until the point when it stops working, as do most things. Those errors are not unrelated - they tell you that the code is
not
working anymore.
For this particular error, seems like modifying the conditional on line 88 could fix it:
JavaScript:
if (matrix[row][col] && (
          // outside the game bounds
          cellCol + col < 0 ||
          cellRow + row < 0 ||
          cellCol + col >= playfield[0].length ||
          cellRow + row >= playfield.length ||
          // collides with another piece
          playfield[cellRow + row][cellCol + col])
        ) {
        return false;
      }
But once again, I'd highly recommend to play with that only after you've finished everything else and have a good project that will work even without the minigame.
